From 509bbb5098ed7fb47dd180cc31efa99690991065 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mminin <mminin2010@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 15:42:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] XFA: Fill gaps in the scripting object model

Scripts of real forms failed on parts of the object model that were
missing; across a corpus of 105 government forms the script errors go
from 529 to 140.

- Form variables (<variables><text name="Version">) resolve by name,
  and script objects are properties of the subform declaring them.
- Script objects shadow the globals: forms define their own util.
- Script objects export the functions and variables declared at their
  top level, found by a scanner that skips comments, strings, regular
  expressions and nested functions, instead of a regular expression
  that also caught nested and commented out functions.
- Scripts outside events see an empty event object, not null.
- Unqualified parent and instanceManager refer to the script's object,
  and xfa.resolveNode() falls back to resolving from it.
- Areas are transparent to SOM names, as unnamed subforms are, and
  names before an index may be followed by spaces ("Row [2]").
- Properties such as assist.speak or border.fill.color are created on
  first use, as for containers.
- clearItems(), addItem(), setItems(), deleteItem(), moveInstance(),
  recalculate(), fillColor, borderColor, fontColor, borderWidth and
  mandatory now work, and xfa.log exists.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
